From 8099cee92c78dd2472749ca8003053ee73be908d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 17:45:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(vllm): support upstream managed-weight loading

Upstream base: 0f3a8cbfd1c11d27f04e3ab37a802d522f4f1c68 plus carries
through de8e7fa971eb7ae4c21e634a8931407a0b404568.
Rationale: B12X master assumes loader coordination and progress interfaces that
are not present in canonical vLLM; GB10 coherent managed allocation needs only
the generic owned-transfer boundary.
Quality: serialized tensor values and destination dtypes are unchanged; unsupported
device/GDS mode fails closed instead of silently taking an unsafe route.
Tests: ruff and py_compile passed; SM121 full-model load and memory audit remain.
Upstream status: local compatibility carry intended for B12X contribution.

---
 b12x/integration/vllm/loader.py | 91 +++++----------------------------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 77 deletions(-)

diff --git a/b12x/integration/vllm/loader.py b/b12x/integration/vllm/loader.py
index 7631910c..1b9563e0 100644
--- a/b12x/integration/vllm/loader.py
+++ b/b12x/integration/vllm/loader.py
